#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:5
#: b27d923482f7494ba375382ea2cea4a1
msgid "MultiCopter Safety"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:9
#: fdb33196a91c44e2b03b896bd250fa41
msgid "Your first priority must be the safety of people!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:11
#: 3bb6f5c7716b447d8060ae28bf6adfd6
msgid "**Crashes can happen, because of pilot error or hardware or software malfunction.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:13
#: 72e68a54017f4cc2b03149185a7dd1a6
msgid "**If you are flying anywhere near other people, you are putting them at risk!**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:16
#: 4ac90feab2de4e3e9f50a952f7fdb0f8
msgid "Be sure to maintain safe distances between yourself, and spectators and your copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:18
#: a5776a52e7664fbf9c2692c7b1603942
msgid "Circumstances will require that you will need to make your own determination of what is a \"safe distance\" from people and property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:21
#: 776e3b4097f34ff68928746735a50987
msgid "At a minimum, consider: at least 10ft (3m) but not further than 30ft (10m) from you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:23
#: 56468072a69546dca60b51f4128e6991
msgid "Keep all other people, property and obstacles considerably further away from your copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:25
#: e35073c006414ecd9483c2100ba2b9d9
msgid "Ensure that no one gets between you and your copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:26
#: 80919dca2eec4533bb4e714415f21a9f
msgid "Spectators should always be a safe distance behind the pilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:27
#: 68f04dbe1a00448a89da87c899161b7f
msgid "If people intrude beyond what you have determined to be the \"safe\" area, land immediately and do not take off until they are clear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:29
#: 81fbc7bc93f2420398dc1d5235a228d2
msgid "At full power, an average sized multi-copter can exceed 20 mph (32 km/h), can ascend to hundreds of feet and easily travel more than a mile in distance before running out of battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:33
#: 2fe87df25025475cb0bca2a89c2c454b
msgid "**If you are flying too high or near airports you are putting manned aircraft and the people on them at risk!**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:36
#: 1cb2faa818754d9ea01f5298d17ff30e
msgid "Get to know where your nearest airports are and do not fly anywhere near them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:39
#: b97cdf1c68704134a6bccb5a1c257544
msgid "**Always ensure the battery cable is NOT connected to the power distribution board or harness until you are ready to fly.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:42
#: be45a3983d2541368423cde80f897350
msgid "Always Turn on the transmitter and ensure the throttle stick is all the way down **BEFORE** connecting the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:44
#: e77928e5269b43028687de30b903819f
msgid "After landing the first thing you should do is disconnect your battery cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:46
#: 879af54b47754c8eb379620683838514
msgid "Do not turn off the transmitter until after you have disconnected the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:48
#: c9c168e331c8408388dfef5946dc50c0
msgid "Always remove your props while you are testing motors, your hands, arms and face and those of your friends will thank you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:50
#: 4a98ba291f69496291b2c3f84bdea35e
msgid "When the battery is connected, always assume the motors are armed; you can check with a short throttle pulse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:52
#: 606f7f232de841938c299db909a1452e
msgid "Don't pick up the model and the radio at the same time, you may bump the throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:54
#: 894e0a7f53cb45f1873aa8c1d318598a
msgid "Do not attempt to fly longer than your battery's safe capacity, it is very bad for the battery and can cause a crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:57
#: fd63a4663e8144f2a6c840f81aeba548
msgid "**ArduPilot includes a motor arming safety feature.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:59
#: f40e9d572ee147ffa1d5c5db557ed119
msgid "Immediately prior to flight after the battery has been connected, the RC transmitter's throttle stick needs to be held down and to the right for several seconds to arm the motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:62
#: b54d304db2744363a1613e32722f54c1
msgid "After landing your first response should be to hold the throttle down and to the left for several seconds to \"Disarm\" the motors. Disarm condition can be tested by moving the throttle stick up, if the motors do not move it is probably disarmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:66
#: 4425dc8791964a76aaaa791df1f74b8a
msgid "Even when disarmed, the throttle stick should always be kept in the full down position except when flying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:69
#: ad9c1f2d940e48019d2789d755112354
msgid "**Get used to switching back to Stabilize mode from other modes and reassuming full manual control.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:72
#: 55dd35e7d3ac44f7bd8f0e6b8c9d3ced
msgid "This is the single most important recovery technique (practice it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:74
#: de355ec1a1b3453c8f7f951c35a4d155
msgid "Stabilize mode can have Simple mode added to it, but if you do you should then practice with it till you are proficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:76
#: fe28f602ff6e4285b9f82aeba6eb5873
msgid "Do not start using any other modes than Stabilize or Stabilize plus Simple until you are VERY comfortable flying your copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:79
#: 8afa791f3a9244bcb446cd447e2b59a1
msgid "**It is very important to have excess power available.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:81
#: 1816230a2d6541728e649690224c26f4
msgid "If you have insufficient power, the automatic controls can require more throttle than is available and destabilization may result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:83
#: e77379a290224e0babe482b8cc830b80
msgid "Ideally your copter should be able to hover at about 50% throttle (mid stick)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:86
#: 4ec4f51fc57f42ac95b71397117fa582
msgid "**Especially while you are learning, it is recommended that you avoid expensive, stiff, ultra-sharp carbon fiber props.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:89
#: 26070d90d7ae417c8cdaee08ee0da31f
msgid "Get cheaper, more flexible and more breakable plastic propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:90
#: dfe61778f8894d208f3a4b8ef61cdc7c
msgid "Some of the super carbon fiber ones can cut better than a Ginsu and while they are almost indestructible - you are not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:93
#: de2238d86cd24ecba0322d186c971c20
msgid "**Important primary response to a crash, inadequate landing or unknown autopilot state.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:96
#: 229a3ef3bd58479eb61e90716c216522
msgid "The first thing to do is throw a towel over your copters propellers (Propellers may start spinning unexpectedly)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:98
#: 763b25aed5f94c989edc831a134e3190
msgid "Then immediately disconnect the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:99
#: 18f36e0694f84d43a4033c089eeda55b
msgid "A large towel is your most important piece of safety equipment followed by a fire extinguisher and a first aid kit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:101
#: e860cacd6a7b4502a9a7e6f3757397fe
msgid "Generally better to use the first one than the last one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:103
#: 442ce5b8853c448692f70fe4cebe16d4
msgid "**When testing or flying any of the (waypoint) navigation modes (using GPS):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:106
#: c3c76bb943ad4594928534a9938ebabb
msgid "Ensure that your GPS has \"Lock\" before arming and takeoff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:107
#: 40143effd1ea4323b0d897669a953ba4
msgid "Check that your home position on the Mission Planner is in fact correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:109
#: bf5ed55f2d0a4f67ad1476b6c9dea2e5
msgid "If the GPS does not accurately report your home position, reboot and wait for 8 or more satellites (not just 3D lock) and check again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:113
#: 7e573dbddd66427e94191c62e81c7a1c
msgid "**Always follow the law:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:115
#: 901cab38809745f69e27e13d5fb7264b
msgid "Our personal use of MultiCopters (models in general) is continually under attack by those who fear 'drones' and invasion of privacy.  If you break the law, or invade someone's privacy, or put them in harm's way, you threaten the future of our personal use of models. Please, understand the law and the rights of others - and fly accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:121
#: 6886ba8280c9459b9933c24859b68ff3
msgid "Most countries have a prominent model aircraft organization. In the USA that is the `AMA <https://www.modelaircraft.org/>`__. Review the AMA `safety code <https://www.modelaircraft.org/sites/default/files/105.pdf>`__. Working with the FAA and other government organizations, the AMA has established (and continues to update) rules for `First Person View (FPV) Operations <https://www.modelaircraft.org/system/files/documents/550.pdf>`__. If you are in the USA (or not), read these documents! The AMA has a strong lobbying group that will help protect our rights. Get involved and support your country's model aircraft organizations - and help protect our right to fly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:133
#: 0580c243ed2440c18fe9ed12218d0f98
msgid "Most important: Keep a safe distance between your Copter and People!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:138
#: 189ca56f019d4eaa951fa26ab932a07e
msgid "These tips can also help protect your multicopter from damage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:141
#: 1d61914668a24b91bad391f05b4115b2
msgid "**Avoid sudden or extreme transmitter control stick deflections.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:143
#: a6c2bd3c2d3642e89cd272e1bd584fe8
msgid "Move the control sticks in small measured increments and don't \"yank\" on them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:145
#: 9d5b9d5f6a62424eab14804971e0e5a1
msgid "If the copter is properly calibrated and balanced it should require only small stick inputs to control altitude, direction and speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:149
#: 3a1ba95cdb5b47c29a8daa963c182ee8
msgid "**Your copter should be more or less stable on the horizontal plane without any control inputs.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:152
#: b078ee5ce35f45d980f91aad7f63762f
msgid "If you are \"fighting\" the copter, land and fix it - something is not right - Hardware adjustment or software calibration may be required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:156
#: 283f44d1a5b04faab599b49c39ccfc5f
msgid "**Be especially careful of large throttle inputs, as a copter can gain (or lose) altitude very rapidly.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:158
#: 0971f14047c84dd79cee08a36e2a4a37
msgid "**Because MultiCopters are symmetrical it is especially easy to lose Visual Orientation.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:161
#: e2df0ebb9a2f43cebb3482afbb6df1c3
msgid "For manual flight modes, maintaining a clear vision of the Copters Orientation (direction it is facing) is the most critical part of successful flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:164
#: c8c29a6e6b194fb2a41d0e1848462207
msgid "Especially while learning it is very important to keep your copter appropriately close to you to aid in maintaining visual orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:167
#: 0ef940a7a616405c9915a6dc822256ec
msgid "Generally: more than 10ft (3m) but not further than 30ft (10m) from you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:169
#: 481ec21665b34e8a83c4cb1b4a582b97
msgid "If the copter gets further than about 100ft (30m) it starts getting difficult to be able to maintain **orientation** and can easily crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:172
#: dfaa48df6c2d4beab82bdee9c2e4c494
msgid "If you lose Yaw orientation while flying in Stabilize mode, try only flying forward and using yaw to steer like a car."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:174
#: 51c3ba9ee34d4edc8278331ac4b1ff9a
msgid "It is much better to simply descend and land rather than have an **orientation-induced** crash or worse still - a **fly away**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:176
#: 2158ce39ff164b54bae12657032a038c
msgid "Fly-Aways often happen when the copter is commanded to tilt back towards the pilot but has rotated in the meantime and is so far away that orientation is lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:179
#: 48aeced7fe424bc69a53ca9f8fbe7906
msgid "Result: the copter flies further away and crashes or is lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:181
#: c954ddb870264d11a3b3f0167446cf4c
msgid "**Always have Stabilize mode as the (Go To) one of your mode switch options.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:183
#: a6a27f43df69498cb96423f597f794e9
msgid "**High or unexpected winds or gusts can make flight considerably more difficult.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:186
#: 21986d84dd754be3b048c16f4346bb31
msgid "High winds can prevent forward progress or spin the copter around causing you to become disoriented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:188
#: c4ae3faef25e449e8d9bd38be21e19fa
msgid "The higher you are, the more likely high winds will be a problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:189
#: c6327360ca7f4f0ea1c139f2aaca9dfc
msgid "Switching to Stabilize mode and landing before you reach your skill limits can help you save your copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:191
#: 6d4d06412c9743b7ad5e469825041bc6
msgid "Avoid flying at high speed or high altitude until you have gained considerable confidence in both manual and automatic modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:193
#: e5681fae08d54650bf1523c123fd2906
msgid "When flying around trees or buildings it is very easy to lose visual orientation or even to lose sight of the copter completely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:195
#: c7b4f546ce8f42d3b7720ad4a4de1ef4
msgid "Gusting winds around objects can also worsen the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:196
#: 77012a7372c6467c8c20b52576b3631f
msgid "Radio signal loss can also occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:197
#: 111914d962564f2a879fa91bb0d02f05
msgid "If your copter is approaching a potentially interfering object, immediately switch to Stabilize mode and land or retrieve the copter to your location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:201
#: b13da8ba4a1b4caaba2d22c7943cf87b
msgid "**ArduPilot specific safety modes: RTL, FailSafe and GeoFence.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:203
#: aeefb34a46164eedbe248099474d2c7a
msgid "RTL can provide a safe **Return to Launch** if it starts to get away from you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:205
#: 180490ab57e6484aadf2c2de206597ec
msgid "Set up a **FailSafe** on Radio Fail with an RTL or Descend response to save your Copter and prevent Injury."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:207
#: 0c00db96255f416c8b9db6b3e5323cb1
msgid "**GeoFence** establishes an automatic flying perimeter that will force your copter to stay in a safe proximity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:209
#: a1bdf285cbbb4a55ac7b6e319498f5a7
msgid "Do not rely solely on the above safety modes, always be ready to take back control in Stabilize and set the copter down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:211
#: 4811ad854af74fdeadf40672691f2de9
msgid "Especially do not rely on the above safety modes to perform maneuvers or training that you would otherwise consider dangerous."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:213
#: 543c0edabd3b44b3815f66b147834e24
msgid "These modes are a supplement to, not a replacement for sound safety practices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:216
#: ce0c75afb5ad4d98845ca9622315424a
msgid "**On your first takeoff after tuning or hardware setup:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:218
#: 31082ea85b4c468eb00dc9481b3ec70a
msgid "In Stabilize mode advance the throttle very slowly until the copter is almost hovering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:220
#: 410d4e5d748c4327b037c0c7b52e94a2
msgid "If the copter is trying to flip over turn it off and correct the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:222
#: 3de490d73722451281a2619440f75886
msgid "A motor could be turning the wrong direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:223
#: 874c604c8eda4d4ebc2da073e3ff4e5e
msgid "Or a wrong direction prop could be installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:224
#: dfba7ddb3fbc4633b2789ac178b7c9c8
msgid "If it tries to rotate on its axis or fly off in some direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:225
#: 10599113ec5a489291647ae872be792c
msgid "The transmitter or RC setup in Mission Planner may be incorrect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:226
#: efa63af60ea945278adf7ca47827bd91
msgid "A motor or ESC may not be performing properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:227
#: 8977edfeb4ef490d90983241ae64892b
msgid "The wrong props may be on the wrong motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:228
#: b0d68e5bc740448e81e7e9a15ec16d59
msgid "When all problems are fixed it should be fairly easy to get the copter to hover a foot or 2 above the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:230
#: 4a0aea89912f41ac8ea2e741ff01fc98
msgid "If a stable and stationary hover a foot or 2 above the ground cannot be achieved, land and fix the problem until it can."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:233
#: ceabc768844249c5a14eb1590bdd34d0
msgid "**When flying FPV \"First Person View\" (with a video camera), Have your modes set to: STABILIZE, SIMPLE, and RTL.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:236
#: 994115f2c7cf492da04f6142bd8bfa8e
msgid "Ensure RTL is working properly before using FPV."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:237
#: 901bd6d527b14b31af7afe6d0fdc85b8
msgid "Use Stabilize mode to fly FPV."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:238
#: 042c2398449b4a2580e8b41879c24444
msgid "If you lose your FPV video, you can switch to Simple or RTL to get back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:241
#: 7b17deb9020b4f46907040875234dcb4
msgid "**Make sure your battery can't fall out.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:243
#: a4590f32750f42d7b47dfc2ed91dc1d1
msgid "Use a Velcro Strap to hold it in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:244
#: 17f3ab3b14d2479086d1b48e6c993c89
msgid "You can also use adhesive backed velcro under the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:248
#: c121bd52858a4481a422fc07a6e6481b
msgid "Get a Printable PDF Safety Sheet: `MultiCopter_Safety <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/pdf_guides/MultiCopter_Safety.pdf>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/safety-multicopter.rst:250
#: c43e6a092de0435bb054af3d0d3e21d0
msgid "The `Copter Forum <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/c/arducopter>`__ permits the developers to respond to your questions and enables you to research similar issues, Please choose the sub-forum that is most appropriate to the wiki page and issues you are having."
msgstr ""
